<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarolt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarolt was a Hungarian noblewoman, daughter of the gyula who ruled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geza-grand-prince-of-the-hungarians">Géza, Grand Prince of the Hungarians</a>. She was the mother of Stephen I, the first king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. The German chronicler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thietmar-of-merseburg">Thietmar of Merseburg</a> described her as a forceful, hard-drinking woman who rode like a warrior and held great influence over her husband's rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarolt.jpg" alt="Sarolt" width="320" height="601" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: photo taken by uploader User:Csanády · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chronicon_Pictum_P037_Szent_Istv%C3%A1n_sz%C3%BClet%C3%A9se.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
